course: dictionary
lesson: 14439
title: The science of ancient life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Palaeontology is a long word, but its first part helps. "Palaeo" means ancient, and "-ontology" means the study of something. So palaeontology is the study of ancient life. In American spelling it is written paleontology, but the meaning is the same.
explain: Use the context to check. «Palaeontologists found the fossil of a dinosaur buried in the rock.» The clues are fossil, dinosaur and rock, so palaeontology must be the science that studies life from long ago.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to test it. «The science of ancient life found the fossil of a dinosaur buried in the rock.» It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: Palaeontology is the science that studies life from long ago.
fact: Most palaeontology is learned from fossils, which are the remains or traces of animals and plants from long ago.
fact: A palaeontologist digs up fossils, cleans them and works out what the animal was like.
fact: Palaeontology also studies how living things changed over millions of years.
fact: Mary Anning was a fossil hunter from Lyme Regis in England, and she found famous fossils in the 1800s.
exercise: «Palaeontology helps us learn about dinosaurs.» What does palaeontology mean? | The study of stars and planets | A shop that sells old furniture | *The science that studies life from long ago | A type of rock climbing
exercise: Who is a palaeontologist? | A cook who makes dinner in a castle | *A scientist who digs up fossils and works out what ancient animals were like | A teacher of maths | A doctor who treats broken bones
exercise: Mary Anning found famous fossils in which place? | *Lyme Regis in England | Paris in France | Glasgow in Scotland | Sydney in Australia
test: What does palaeontology study? | Stars that shine at night | Clouds and weather | Ancient coins only | *Life from long ago, mostly through fossils
test: What is a fossil? | *The remains or traces of an animal or plant from long ago | A kind of sweet drink | A fresh apple from the shop | A type of modern computer
exam: Ben says palaeontology is about making pottery. Which answer is correct? | Palaeontology is the study of the weather | *Palaeontology is the science that studies life from long ago, through fossils | Palaeontology means a very small insect | Pottery is the main job of a palaeontologist
